+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# STAGE-2 DNA CONVERGENCE (2026-08-01) — the KIT axis, adopted word for word from
+# station_pillar.gd / station_crates.gd / station_wall.gd. Read one of those blocks
+# too; the four of them are one promotion with four bodies.
+#
+# This artifact's truth line ends "a lit bay is never quite empty" — a claim about
+# a room being INHABITED. But the fixture had no time of its own. Every one of its
+# 47 placements renders the same instant: commissioned, lamped, powered, aimed. A
+# light that can only ever be on cannot say anything about whether anyone is still
+# working here; it can only say the room was handed over.
+#
+#   upkeep   WHICH MOMENT of the working life   service · works · store · scrap
+#
+#   service  in commission — the legacy lineage, byte for byte
+#   works    mid-job       — lens out on a step trestle, open bore, gear tray, loom, WORKS
+#   store    packed down   — head bagged and banded, post sleeved, lens covered, SEALED
+#   scrap    robbed        — head cut off the arm, wire tails, the shade down on the floor
+#
+# The LENS is the pivot, exactly as the groove is on the pillar and the lit seam on
+# the wall: it is the only emissive surface on the piece and it owns the brightest
+# pixels in any frame the luminaire appears in. `works` moves it to a trestle,
+# `store` buries it under the bag and `scrap` leaves it broken on the floor — three
+# different places for the hottest thing in the shot, legible from across a room
+# rather than only under measurement.
+#
+# The REAL light rides the same gate. A bagged or robbed fixture that still threw a
+# full pool would be the one dishonest thing in the kit, so `_powered()` drops
+# light_energy to 0 for `store` and `scrap`. It is an APPEARANCE change (nothing
+# here is a hazard, a trigger or a traversal dependency), but it is the one value in
+# this promotion that reaches past the mesh, and an author who dims a bay's only
+# fixture is choosing to. `service` and `works` are both powered, so the default is
+# untouched and a map lit by luminaires stays lit.
+#
+# Deliberately NOT routed through upkeep: `height`, `arm_reach` and `mode`. The
+# composer matches those to the bay being lit, so a value that moved the envelope
+# would take the fixture out of the cell it was placed in. Upkeep dresses the
+# luminaire; it never re-sites it.
+# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
 @export_group("Mode")
